<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0"
         xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 https://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">
    <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>

    <!--
        carddemo-batch — batch orchestration layer of the hexagonal architecture
        (AAP §0.3.1, §0.3.6).

        Contents:
          * BatchRunContext record + ScopedValue<BatchRunContext> declaration —
            propagates run ID, processing date, and tenant through the entire
            dynamic call scope including child virtual threads, replacing the
            ThreadLocal idiom entirely (AAP §0.6.6, §0.6.7; JEP 506 Final).
          * Batch driver classes that compose use cases from carddemo-application:
              - PostTransactionsBatch       (composes CbTrn02C — POSTTRAN JCL)
              - InterestCalculationBatch    (composes CbAct04C — INTCALC JCL)
              - DailyRejectsBatch           (composes CbTrn02C rejects — DALYREJS JCL)
              - PrintTcatBalBatch           (composes account/category dump — PRTCATBL JCL)
              - CombineTransactionsBatch    (composes CbTrn01C — COMBTRAN JCL)
              - CreateStatementsBatch       (composes CbStm03A — CREASTMT JCL)
            (AAP §0.3.1 layout, §0.4.1 file-by-file plan)
          * Virtual-thread fan-out via Executors.newVirtualThreadPerTaskExecutor()
            ONLY where per-record work is provably independent and reordering
            does NOT change observable output. Sort orders and record sequencing
            are preserved (AAP §0.1.3, §0.6.6).

        Architectural rule (AAP §0.3.6, §0.6.12):
          * This module depends on carddemo-application (use-case ring) and
            transitively on carddemo-domain (innermost ring).
          * This module is depended on by carddemo-app (composition root) — never
            the reverse.
          * The composition root (carddemo-app) wires file/db adapters at startup
            and invokes batch drivers in this module; this module must NOT depend
            on carddemo-adapter-file, carddemo-adapter-db, carddemo-app, or
            carddemo-tests.

        Forbidden here (AAP §0.1.1 architectural override, §0.6.7, §0.6.12, §0.7.4):
          * Spring Batch — AAP §0.6.12 explicit override (the previously planned
            Spring Batch 5.x architecture documented in docs/technical-specifications.md
            is REPLACED by plain Java drivers with virtual-thread fan-out and
            ScopedValue propagation).
          * Spring / Spring Boot / Spring Data / Spring Security / Spring MVC /
            Spring Cloud AWS — plain constructor injection only.
          * Hibernate / JPA / jakarta.persistence / javax.persistence
          * Lombok — Java 25 records replace it.
          * JDBC drivers (PostgreSQL, MySQL, DB2, H2) — those belong to
            carddemo-adapter-db.
          * Flyway, Liquibase, Testcontainers, LocalStack
          * Micrometer, Prometheus, OpenTelemetry, Jaeger
          * jqwik (property tests live in carddemo-tests per AAP §0.3.1)
          * maven-shade-plugin — shading is configured per-executable in
            carddemo-app/pom.xml only (AAP §0.4.1).
          * The "enable-preview" JVM flag (AAP §0.7.4 — finalized JEPs only:
            JEP 506 ScopedValue, JEP 510 KDF, JEP 511 Module Import, JEP 513
            Flexible Constructor Bodies, JEP 519 Compact Headers, JEP 521
            Generational Shenandoah). ThreadLocal is FORBIDDEN; ScopedValue
            replaces it entirely per AAP §0.6.6.
          * &lt;source&gt;/&lt;target&gt; tags — the parent POM's &lt;release&gt;25&lt;/release&gt;
            is the single source of truth for the Java language level.
    -->

    <parent>
        <groupId>com.blitzy.carddemo</groupId>
        <artifactId>carddemo-parent</artifactId>
        <version>1.0.0-SNAPSHOT</version>
        <relativePath>../pom.xml</relativePath>
    </parent>

    <artifactId>carddemo-batch</artifactId>
    <packaging>jar</packaging>

    <name>CardDemo Batch</name>
    <description>
        Batch orchestration layer of the hexagonal architecture: composes use
        cases from carddemo-application, applies virtual-thread fan-out where
        reordering does NOT change observable output, and declares
        ScopedValue&lt;BatchRunContext&gt; for batch-run context propagation
        (run ID, processing date, tenant). NO Spring Batch, NO framework —
        plain Java drivers per AAP §0.6.12 architectural override. ThreadLocal
        is FORBIDDEN; ScopedValue (JEP 506 Final) replaces it entirely per
        AAP §0.6.6 and §0.6.7. Depends on carddemo-application (which
        transitively depends on carddemo-domain).
    </description>

    <dependencies>
        <!--
            Internal dependency: carddemo-application — the core use-case layer.
            Provides one Java class per COBOL PROGRAM-ID from app/cbl/ that this
            batch module composes and orchestrates:
              * CbTrn02C — full posting engine (composed by PostTransactionsBatch
                and DailyRejectsBatch, driven by POSTTRAN/DALYREJS JCL)
              * CbAct04C — interest calculation engine (composed by
                InterestCalculationBatch, driven by INTCALC JCL)
              * CbStm03A — statement generation (composed by
                CreateStatementsBatch, driven by CREASTMT JCL)
              * CbStm03B — callable file-services subroutine (utility for
                statement generation)
              * CbTrn01C — daily transaction loader (composed by
                CombineTransactionsBatch, driven by COMBTRAN JCL)
              * CbTrn03C — paginated transaction detail report writer
              * CbAct01C / CbAct02C / CbAct03C / CbCus01C — sequential
                file readers used by dump and verification batch flows
              * ProgramRegistry — dynamic CALL routing for COBOL CALL with a
                variable program name (AAP §0.3.2)
            Version inherited from the parent POM's dependencyManagement
            (${project.version} = 1.0.0-SNAPSHOT).
            This is the core internal dependency of this orchestration layer
            per AAP §0.4.1 and §0.6.12.
        -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>com.blitzy.carddemo</groupId>
            <artifactId>carddemo-application</artifactId>
        </dependency>

        <!--
            Internal dependency: carddemo-domain — innermost ring of the
            hexagonal architecture. Although reachable TRANSITIVELY through
            carddemo-application above, declared explicitly per AAP §0.4.1 and
            the file's agent_prompt §1.2 for intent clarity to readers and
            tooling.
            Provides:
              * Java records (AccountRecord, TranRecord, DalyTranRecord,
                CardDemoCommarea, TranCatBalRecord, etc.) used by batch drivers
                for run-context records, fan-out parameter records, and
                reject-record encoding (AAP §0.6.9)
              * Sealed types (UserType, PgmContext, AidKey, FileStatus, etc.)
                from REDEFINES and 88-level value-space taxonomies (AAP §0.6.10)
              * Repository port interfaces (AccountRepository, CardRepository,
                TransactionRepository, DailyTransactionRepository, etc.) —
                ports the batch drivers wire to adapter implementations at the
                composition root (AAP §0.3.1)
              * Decimals utility — BigDecimal facade with MathContext.DECIMAL128
                and RoundingMode selection used for any monetary aggregation in
                batch drivers (AAP §0.3.3, §0.6.1)
              * @CobolProgram traceability annotation cited in Javadoc on every
                translated class (AAP §0.2.1)
            Version inherited from the parent POM's dependencyManagement
            (${project.version} = 1.0.0-SNAPSHOT).
        -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>com.blitzy.carddemo</groupId>
            <artifactId>carddemo-domain</artifactId>
        </dependency>

        <!--
            Production dependency: SLF4J API only (compile scope).
            Used by batch drivers in this module to emit structured log
            messages for:
              * Run start/end events (BatchRunContext binding/unbinding)
              * Fan-out parameters (record counts, parallelism degree,
                virtual-thread executor lifecycle events)
              * FILE STATUS-equivalent exception summaries (sealed
                FileStatus hierarchy mapped to typed exceptions per AAP §0.6.10)
              * Reject-counter snapshots (rejected vs posted transaction counts
                from CbTrn02C DALYREJS flow)
              * ScopedValue<BatchRunContext> bindings (run ID, processing date,
                tenant) per AAP §0.6.6 and §0.6.12
              * PAN-masking enforcement (mask all but last 4 digits per
                AAP §0.7.2)
            The runtime implementation (logback-classic) is supplied by the
            composition root (carddemo-app); this module depends only on the
            API, keeping the orchestration layer free of concrete logging
            dependencies per AAP §0.6.12.
            Version is inherited from the parent POM's dependencyManagement
            (slf4j-api 2.0.16 per AAP §0.5.1).
        -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.slf4j</groupId>
            <artifactId>slf4j-api</artifactId>
        </dependency>

        <!--
            Test dependencies (test scope only).
            Versions are inherited from the parent POM's dependencyManagement:
              * junit-jupiter            via junit-bom 5.13.1 (AAP §0.5.1) —
                                            unit tests for batch drivers asserting
                                            virtual-thread fan-out invariants
                                            (preserved sort order, no record
                                            reordering), ScopedValue<BatchRunContext>
                                            binding/get behavior, batch composition
                                            wiring, and reject-vs-post counter
                                            assertions per AAP §0.6.6
              * junit-platform-launcher  1.13.1 — required minimum for
                                            JUnit Platform native discovery by
                                            maven-surefire-plugin 3.5.2 and
                                            aligns with jqwik 1.9.3's minimum
                                            platform requirement to ensure
                                            consistent JUnit Platform version
                                            across the multi-module build
                                            (AAP §0.5.1)
              * assertj-core             3.26.3 — fluent assertions for
                                            batch-run counter values,
                                            reject-record lists, and
                                            ScopedValue propagation outcomes
                                            (AAP §0.5.1)
            Note: jqwik is NOT declared here — property-based tests for the
            Decimals utility live in carddemo-tests per AAP §0.3.1.
        -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.junit.jupiter</groupId>
            <artifactId>junit-jupiter</artifactId>
            <scope>test</scope>
        </dependency>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.junit.platform</groupId>
            <artifactId>junit-platform-launcher</artifactId>
            <scope>test</scope>
        </dependency>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.assertj</groupId>
            <artifactId>assertj-core</artifactId>
            <scope>test</scope>
        </dependency>
    </dependencies>

    <build>
        <plugins>
            <!--
                maven-compiler-plugin — activated for this module so the parent's
                pluginManagement (version 3.13.0, &lt;release&gt;25&lt;/release&gt;, no
                preview flag per AAP §0.7.4, -parameters for record component
                names) applies during the compile phase. The Java language
                level is set ONCE in the parent POM; this child must not
                redeclare &lt;source&gt;, &lt;target&gt;, or &lt;release&gt;.
            -->
            <plugin>
                <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
                <artifactId>maven-compiler-plugin</artifactId>
            </plugin>

            <!--
                maven-surefire-plugin — activated for this module so the parent's
                pluginManagement (version 3.5.2, JUnit Platform native discovery,
                no "enable-preview" argLine per AAP §0.7.4) applies during the
                test phase. Test classes are discovered by the standard
                **/*Test.java and **/*Tests.java patterns.
            -->
            <plugin>
                <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
                <artifactId>maven-surefire-plugin</artifactId>
            </plugin>
        </plugins>
    </build>
</project>
